-- g2-tests-art5.l4: tests of Article 5, every expected value decided from the Law's text before the module was run.
-- The charity test (5(1)(a), 5(1)(b), 5(2), 5(3)), the guidance duties (5(4) to 5(8)), and the forks F2.1, F2.2, F2.3, F2.4, F2.6, F2.7.

§ `Tests of Article 5`

§§ `Cases`

-- The purposes of a case, each with the facts that Article 6 reads.
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: education` MEANS `the G2 pair of a purpose with nothing relevant recorded under` `the advancement of education`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: poverty` MEANS `the G2 pair of a purpose with nothing relevant recorded under` `the prevention or relief of poverty`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: ancillary` MEANS `the G2 purpose` `a G2 ancillary purpose` `with` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: no head` MEANS `the G2 purpose` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `with` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: political` MEANS `the G2 purpose` `a G2 political purpose` `with` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: political and flagged ancillary` MEANS `the G2 purpose` `a G2 political purpose that is also flagged ancillary` `with` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: a philosophical belief` MEANS `the G2 purpose` `a G2 purpose of advancing a philosophical belief` `with` `G2 facts: nothing relevant`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: sport without physical skill and exertion` MEANS `the G2 purpose` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of public participation in sport`) `with` `G2 facts: a pastime that involves no physical skill and exertion`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: sport with physical skill and exertion` MEANS `the G2 purpose` (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of public participation in sport`) `with` `G2 facts: a sport that involves physical skill and exertion`
GIVETH A `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
`pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need` MEANS `the G2 purpose` `a G2 purpose that falls under no head` `with` `G2 facts: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`

-- The constitutions of a case.
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`no permission` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits nothing of the kinds Article 5(2) names`
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`governor may be the Chief Minister acting as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `a Minister who holds the office of the Chief Minister` `with the capacity` TRUE
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`control by the Chief Minister acting as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` `by` `a Minister who holds the office of the Chief Minister` `with the capacity` TRUE
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`governor may be the Chief Minister, not as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `a Minister who holds the office of the Chief Minister` `with the capacity` FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`governor may be the Minister for External Relations acting as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `a Minister who holds the office of Minister for External Relations` `with the capacity` TRUE
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`governor may be the Minister for Health acting as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `a Minister who holds another ministerial office, the Minister for Health, say` `with the capacity` TRUE
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`governor may be a member of the States Assembly acting as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `a member of the States Assembly` `with the capacity` TRUE
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`control by a member of the States Assembly acting as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `the activities of the entity to be directed or otherwise controlled by` `by` `a member of the States Assembly` `with the capacity` TRUE
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`governor may be a member of the States Assembly, not as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `a member of the States Assembly` `with the capacity` FALSE
GIVETH A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
`governor may be an equivalent in another jurisdiction acting as such` MEANS `a G2 constitution that expressly permits` `any of the governors of the entity to be` `by` `any equivalent of a Minister or of a member of the States Assembly in another jurisdiction` `with the capacity` TRUE

-- The case: interpretation, standing, purposes with facts, constitution, office of the Minister, determination, Order.
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
      constitution IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      office IS AN `Office of the Minister`
      determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the case meets the charity test` interp standing pfs constitution office determination order MEANS
    `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` interp (`a G2 entity with standing` standing `and these G2 purposes` (`the G2 purposes in` pfs)) pfs constitution office determination order

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
      constitution IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      office IS AN `Office of the Minister`
      determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Limb of the charity test that decides it`
`the limb that decides the case` interp standing pfs constitution office determination order MEANS
    `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` interp (`a G2 entity with standing` standing `and these G2 purposes` (`the G2 purposes in` pfs)) pfs constitution office determination order

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
      constitution IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      office IS AN `Office of the Minister`
      determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the case meets the test only by virtue of an Order` interp standing pfs constitution office determination order MEANS
    `Art 5(3) the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` interp (`a G2 entity with standing` standing `and these G2 purposes` (`the G2 purposes in` pfs)) pfs constitution office determination order

-- The same cases for a body that is not an entity (no kind of entity under Article 2(1)).
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
      constitution IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      office IS AN `Office of the Minister`
      determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the non-entity case meets the charity test` interp standing pfs constitution office determination order MEANS
    `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` interp (`a G2 non-entity standing as` standing `holding these G2 purposes` (`the G2 purposes in` pfs)) pfs constitution office determination order

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
      constitution IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      office IS AN `Office of the Minister`
      determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Limb of the charity test that decides it`
`the limb that decides the non-entity case` interp standing pfs constitution office determination order MEANS
    `Art 5 the limb that decides the charity test` interp (`a G2 non-entity standing as` standing `holding these G2 purposes` (`the G2 purposes in` pfs)) pfs constitution office determination order

GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 3 to 7`
      standing IS A `Standing on the register`
      pfs IS A LIST OF `Purpose with the facts Article 6 reads`
      constitution IS A `Facts about the constitution under Article 5(2)`
      office IS AN `Office of the Minister`
      determination IS A `Determination of public benefit`
      order IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the non-entity case meets the test only by virtue of an Order` interp standing pfs constitution office determination order MEANS
    `Art 5(3) the entity meets the charity test only by virtue of an Order` interp (`a G2 non-entity standing as` standing `holding these G2 purposes` (`the G2 purposes in` pfs)) pfs constitution office determination order

GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` MEANS
    `a proper determination that the entity provides public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`the proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit` MEANS
    `a proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`the proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit` MEANS
    `a proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`
GIVETH A `Determination of public benefit`
`the determination made by presuming public benefit` MEANS
    `a determination that provides public benefit by presuming a charitable purpose to be for the public benefit, made by` `the Commissioner`

§§ `Article 5(1): the charity test`

-- src:145 | (1) An entity meets the charity test if –
-- src:146 | (a) all of its purposes are –
-- src:147 | (i) charitable purposes, or
-- src:148 | (ii) purposes that are purely ancillary or incidental to any of its charitable purposes; and
-- src:149 | (b) in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree.
-- A purely educational entity with a proper determination of public benefit and no constitutional bar meets the test.
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `none: the entity meets the charity test`
-- Two charitable purposes, and an ancillary one beside them.
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: poverty`, `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
-- (a) fails: a purpose that is neither charitable nor ancillary.
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: no head`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
-- (b) fails: a proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit.
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit` FALSE
-- Both (a) and (b) fail: the first limb in the text's order decides.
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: no head`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: a purpose is neither a charitable purpose nor purely ancillary or incidental to one` (LIST (`a G2 purpose that falls under no head`))
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(b) is not met: the entity does not provide public benefit to a reasonable degree`
-- An applicant that intends to provide public benefit meets (b); an entity that is not an applicant must provide it.
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an applicant for registration` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `entered in the general section` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity intends to provide public benefit` FALSE

§§ `Article 6(5) and Article 5(1)(a)(ii): a political purpose is neither charitable nor ancillary`

-- src:148 | (ii) purposes that are purely ancillary or incidental to any of its charitable purposes; and
-- src:201 | (5) The purpose of advancing a political party or promoting a candidate for election to any office, whether in Jersey or elsewhere, is neither a charitable purpose nor a purpose ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose, irrespective of whether it would otherwise fall within paragraph (1) or Article 5(1)(a)(ii).
-- A political purpose alone fails (a).
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: political`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
-- A political purpose beside an educational one fails (a): "all of its purposes".
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: political`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
-- A political purpose flagged ancillary does not count as ancillary: 6(5) overrides 5(1)(a)(ii) by its own words.
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: political and flagged ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(1)(a)(ii) the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose` `pf: political and flagged ancillary`
#ASSERT `Art 5(1)(a)(ii) the purpose is purely ancillary or incidental to a charitable purpose` `pf: ancillary`
-- The limb that decides names the offending purpose.
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: political and flagged ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: a purpose is neither a charitable purpose nor purely ancillary or incidental to one` (LIST (`a G2 political purpose that is also flagged ancillary`))

§§ `Article 6(2) reached through the charity test`

-- src:189 | (c) in paragraph (1)(h), “sport” means sport that involves physical skill and exertion;
-- A sport without physical skill and exertion is not within head (h), so the entity fails (a).
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: sport without physical skill and exertion`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: sport with physical skill and exertion`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
-- src:194 | (f) for the purposes of paragraph (1)(p), the advancement of any philosophical belief (whether or not involving belief in a god) is analogous to the purpose set out in paragraph (1)(c).
-- A purpose of advancing a philosophical belief is a charitable purpose (analogous, 6(2)(f)), on either reading of F2.5.
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: a philosophical belief`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.5 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: a philosophical belief`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE

-- src:193 | (e) paragraph (1)(n) includes relief given by the provision of accommodation or care;
-- FORK F2.14 (Article 6(2)(e)), default ruled by the owner (Meng), 2026-10-27.  An entity whose only purpose is the provision of accommodation or care, with nobody shown to be in need: on reading A the
-- purpose is not a charitable purpose, so (a) fails and that is the limb that decides; on reading B head (n) is engaged, so the entity meets the test.
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: a purpose is neither a charitable purpose nor purely ancillary or incidental to one` (LIST (`a G2 purpose that falls under no head`))
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `none: the entity meets the charity test`

-- src:149 | (b) in giving effect to those purposes, it provides (or, in the case of an applicant, provides or intends to provide) public benefit in Jersey or elsewhere to a reasonable degree.
-- Public benefit is a separate limb.  Even on reading B, where the purpose is within head (n), the entity meets the test only if it also provides public benefit to a reasonable degree (Article 5(1)(b)):
-- a determination that it does not, fails the test and the limb that decides is (b).
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity does not provide public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(b) is not met: the entity does not provide public benefit to a reasonable degree`
-- The determiner's duties still apply on reading B: a determination made without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), or to undue restriction under 7(2)(b), or by presuming the purpose to be for the public
-- benefit (7(3)(a)), does not answer the question, so the test is not decided.
#ASSERT REFUSED `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` (`a determination that provides public benefit without regard to the comparison of 7(2)(a), made by` `the Commissioner`) FALSE BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` (`a determination that provides public benefit for a section of the public without regard to undue restriction, made by` `the Commissioner`) FALSE BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"
#ASSERT REFUSED `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.14 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: the provision of accommodation or care, nobody shown to be in need`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the determination made by presuming public benefit` FALSE BECAUSE "a determination made in breach of the duties on its maker does not answer the question whether the entity provides public benefit"

§§ `FORK F2.1: "all of its purposes" with no purposes, and with ancillary purposes alone`

-- src:146 | (a) all of its purposes are –
-- src:147 | (i) charitable purposes, or
-- src:148 | (ii) purposes that are purely ancillary or incidental to any of its charitable purposes; and
-- The discriminating cases.  Empty purposes: first reading fails (a charitable purpose is required), second and third are satisfied vacuously.
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` EMPTY `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` `not on the register` EMPTY `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` `not on the register` EMPTY `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` EMPTY `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: the entity has no charitable purpose`
-- An ancillary purpose alone: the first and second readings fail it (there is no charitable purpose for it to be ancillary to), the third accepts it.
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
-- The limb that decides names the cause: no charitable purpose, not an offending purpose, for an ancillary purpose alone.
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: the entity has no charitable purpose`
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `Article 5(1)(a) is not met: the entity has no charitable purpose`
#ASSERT `the limb that decides the case` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE EQUALS `none: the entity meets the charity test`
-- Beside a charitable purpose an ancillary purpose counts on every reading.
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
-- A political purpose fails (a) on every reading, even beside charitable ones and even if flagged ancillary.
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as C` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`, `pf: political and flagged ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: political and flagged ancillary`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE

§§ `The facts must be the entity's purposes`

-- Facts for other purposes than the entity's: the encoding refuses rather than test the wrong list.
GIVETH AN Entity
`an entity whose only purpose is education` MEANS `a G2 entity with these purposes` (LIST (`a G2 purpose recorded under` `the advancement of education`))

#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 5 the entity meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an entity whose only purpose is education` (LIST `pf: poverty`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE BECAUSE "the purposes with their Article 6 facts are not the purposes of the entity"
#ASSERT REFUSED `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an entity whose only purpose is education` EMPTY BECAUSE "the purposes with their Article 6 facts are not the purposes of the entity"
#ASSERT `Art 5(1)(a) all of the entity's purposes are charitable or purely ancillary` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `an entity whose only purpose is education` (LIST `pf: education`)

§§ `Article 5(1): a body that is not an entity does not meet the charity test`

-- src:145 | (1) An entity meets the charity test if –
-- Article 5(1) states the test for "an entity".  A body that falls within none of the sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) (a partnership, say) is not an entity, so it does not meet the test, whatever its purposes.
-- It is FALSE, not a refusal.  The control for each case is the same inputs on a company, which are met.
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the non-entity case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `not on the register` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the non-entity case meets the charity test` `the favoured interpretation of Articles 3 to 7` `entered in the general section` (LIST `pf: education`) `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 5(1) the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` (`a G2 entity with these purposes` EMPTY)
#ASSERT NOT `Art 5(1) the body is an entity within Article 2(1)` (`a G2 non-entity standing as` `not on the register` `holding these G2 purposes` EMPTY)
-- No purposes: the second reading of F2.1 would find (a) vacuously satisfied for an entity, and the body is still not an entity.
#ASSERT `the case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` `not on the register` EMPTY `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
#ASSERT NOT `the non-entity case meets the charity test` `the interpretation of Articles 3 to 7 with F2.1 read as B` `not on the register` EMPTY `no permission` `the Chief Minister` `the proper determination that the entity provides public benefit` FALSE
-- A constitution that would bar an entity, with an Order disapplying the bar: an entity then meets the test, a body that is not an entity still does not.
